# Subagent model preference

When delegating **implementation / multi-file coding / refactors / bugfixes**, prefer the custom project subagent **`implementer`** (`.cursor/agents/implementer.md`) instead of built-in `generalPurpose` or spawning Task with Sonnet/Opus.

- That agent is pinned to **`composer-2.5[fast=false]`** (standard Composer 2.5, not fast).
- Do **not** pass an inline Task `model` of `claude-*-sonnet` / Opus for routine implementation unless the user explicitly asks for that model.
- Built-in Explore may still be used for read-only codebase search; it has its own model defaults.

## Why

Built-in Task `model` slugs often only expose `composer-2.5-fast`. Custom subagent frontmatter supports `composer-2.5[fast=false]` so implementation stays on standard Composer 2.5 at lower cost than Sonnet.
